Link ws2_32 on Windows

CascFiles.cpp asks for Winsock with #pragma comment(lib, "ws2_32.lib"), which
only MSVC honours, and common/Sockets.cpp calls socket(), connect(), send(),
recv(), closesocket(), getaddrinfo(), WSAStartup() and WSAGetLastError().
Under MinGW nothing links ws2_32, so those references stay unresolved:
CascLib.dll cannot link, and a program linking the static library fails with

    undefined reference to `__imp_closesocket'

and the rest of those calls. Add ws2_32 to LINK_LIBS next to wininet, which is
already listed there for Windows.

CascLib distributes this file with CRLF line endings; the PKGBUILD strips them
before applying the patch.

Upstream: not submitted yet
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@
 
 set(PUBLIC_COMPILE_DEFINITIONS CASCLIB_NO_AUTO_LINK_LIBRARY CASCLIB_NODEBUG)
 if(WIN32)
-    list(APPEND LINK_LIBS wininet)
+    list(APPEND LINK_LIBS wininet ws2_32)
     if(CASC_UNICODE)
         message(STATUS "Build UNICODE version")
         add_definitions(-DUNICODE -D_UNICODE)
